1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,111
Transition questions look easy.

2
00:00:02,147 --> 00:00:05,127
One blank, four short
choices like however,

3
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:07,984
therefore, and for example.

4
00:00:08,004 --> 00:00:10,947
But they're easy to miss,
because if you plug each word in,

5
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:13,325
two or three of them can sound fine.

6
00:00:13,358 --> 00:00:17,322
The fix is to decide what the blank
needs before you look at the choices.

7
00:00:17,572 --> 00:00:21,373
In this video: the seven
relationships transitions show,

8
00:00:21,393 --> 00:00:24,215
the words in each group, a simple method,

9
00:00:24,286 --> 00:00:28,464
and seven SAT-style questions,
including the traps.

10
00:00:28,484 --> 00:00:30,857
A transition doesn't add information.

11
00:00:30,877 --> 00:00:34,162
It tells you how two ideas connect.

12
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:37,785
So the real question is: what's the
relationship between the sentence before the

13
00:00:37,805 --> 00:00:39,733
blank and the sentence after it?

14
00:00:39,755 --> 00:00:41,612
There are seven to know.

15
00:00:41,683 --> 00:00:43,377
One: contrast.

16
00:00:43,397 --> 00:00:45,663
The next idea goes against the last one.

17
00:00:45,683 --> 00:00:48,913
However, but, yet, in
contrast, by contrast,

18
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:49,949
on the other hand.

19
00:00:49,969 --> 00:00:51,841
Concession is a close cousin.

20
00:00:51,861 --> 00:00:55,592
Nevertheless, nonetheless, even so, still.

21
00:00:55,612 --> 00:00:57,753
It means: despite that.

22
00:00:57,773 --> 00:00:59,915
Two: cause and effect.

23
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,645
The next idea is a result.

24
00:01:01,665 --> 00:01:04,717
Therefore, thus,
consequently, as a result,

25
00:01:04,737 --> 00:01:05,987
for this reason.

26
00:01:06,165 --> 00:01:07,773
Three: addition.

27
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:09,610
More of the same kind of point.

28
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:12,753
Moreover, furthermore,
additionally, in addition,

29
00:01:12,773 --> 00:01:13,808
also.

30
00:01:13,915 --> 00:01:17,058
Similarly and likewise
add a parallel case.

31
00:01:17,133 --> 00:01:18,812
Four: example.

32
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:22,827
The next sentence is a specific
case of a general claim.

33
00:01:22,847 --> 00:01:25,561
For example, for instance, to illustrate.

34
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:28,470
Five: sequence or time.

35
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:32,256
First, next, then, later, subsequently,

36
00:01:32,276 --> 00:01:34,026
meanwhile, finally.

37
00:01:34,092 --> 00:01:36,358
Six: emphasis or clarification.

38
00:01:36,378 --> 00:01:39,429
In fact and indeed push
the same idea further.

39
00:01:39,449 --> 00:01:42,501
In other words and that is
restate it more clearly.

40
00:01:42,521 --> 00:01:44,377
Seven: conclusion.

41
00:01:44,413 --> 00:01:48,650
In conclusion, in sum, in short, overall.

42
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:50,363
You don't need to memorize every word.

43
00:01:50,383 --> 00:01:53,114
You need to know which
group each one belongs to,

44
00:01:53,134 --> 00:01:56,955
because the SAT is really
asking which group fits.

45
00:01:57,023 --> 00:01:58,146
Here's the format.

46
00:01:58,166 --> 00:02:02,539
A short passage with a blank, often
at the start of the last sentence.

47
00:02:02,559 --> 00:02:07,003
The question says: which choice
completes the text with the most logical

48
00:02:07,023 --> 00:02:07,967
transition?

49
00:02:07,987 --> 00:02:11,967
To answer it, read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

50
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:13,681
Sometimes you need the whole passage,

51
00:02:13,701 --> 00:02:16,951
because the last sentence can
connect back to an earlier one.

52
00:02:16,987 --> 00:02:19,253
And watch how fragile the logic is.

53
00:02:19,273 --> 00:02:20,824
The trail was steep.

54
00:02:20,844 --> 00:02:23,752
blank the hikers moved slowly.

55
00:02:23,772 --> 00:02:25,773
That's cause and effect: therefore.

56
00:02:25,806 --> 00:02:27,556
Now change one word.

57
00:02:28,056 --> 00:02:30,021
The trail was steep.

58
00:02:30,235 --> 00:02:32,402
blank the hikers moved quickly.

59
00:02:32,422 --> 00:02:34,438
Now it's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

60
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:35,224
however.

61
00:02:35,244 --> 00:02:39,065
Same sentences, one word different,
and the transition flips.

62
00:02:39,121 --> 00:02:40,335
So here's the method.

63
00:02:40,371 --> 00:02:42,493
Step one: cover the choices.

64
00:02:42,513 --> 00:02:43,887
Don't look at them yet.

65
00:02:43,907 --> 00:02:48,344
Step two: read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

66
00:02:48,364 --> 00:02:52,113
Step three: name the
relationship in a word or two.

67
00:02:52,150 --> 00:02:53,094
Against?

68
00:02:53,114 --> 00:02:54,023
Result?

69
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:55,166
More of the same?

70
00:02:55,186 --> 00:02:56,308
An example?

71
00:02:56,328 --> 00:02:57,629
Later in time?

72
00:02:57,649 --> 00:03:01,558
Step four: uncover the choices,
find the one from that group,

73
00:03:01,578 --> 00:03:04,614
and read the sentence with it
in place to make sure it works.

74
00:03:04,663 --> 00:03:05,663
Let's try it.

75
00:03:05,948 --> 00:03:10,500
Venus is sometimes called Earth's twin
because the two planets are similar in

76
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,162
size and structure.

77
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:16,143
blank the surface of Venus
is far hotter than Earth's:

78
00:03:16,163 --> 00:03:18,448
it is hot enough to melt lead.

79
00:03:18,501 --> 00:03:19,858
Pause and try it.

80
00:03:23,102 --> 00:03:26,225
Before the blank: Venus is like Earth.

81
00:03:26,245 --> 00:03:28,189
After it: Venus is very different.

82
00:03:28,209 --> 00:03:29,153
That's a contrast.

83
00:03:29,173 --> 00:03:31,245
Predict: however, or but.

84
00:03:31,708 --> 00:03:33,268
The answer is A, however.

85
00:03:33,288 --> 00:03:36,518
Similarly would mean
Venus is like Earth again.

86
00:03:36,538 --> 00:03:40,716
Therefore would mean being
Earth's twin causes the heat.

87
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:44,304
And the heat isn't an example
of the two planets being alike,

88
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:46,953
so for example doesn't work either.

89
00:03:46,973 --> 00:03:48,096
Question two.

90
00:03:48,116 --> 00:03:53,846
Unlike most substances, water is less
dense in its solid form than in its liquid

91
00:03:53,866 --> 00:03:54,623
form.

92
00:03:54,643 --> 00:03:59,989
blank ice floats on the surface of lakes
and ponds instead of sinking to the

93
00:04:00,009 --> 00:04:00,732
bottom.

94
00:04:00,752 --> 00:04:02,109
Pause and try it.

95
00:04:05,353 --> 00:04:09,066
Before: solid water is less
dense than liquid water.

96
00:04:09,103 --> 00:04:11,139
After: ice floats.

97
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:14,940
Things that are less dense float, so
the second sentence is the result of the

98
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,761
first.

99
00:04:15,781 --> 00:04:18,403
Predict: therefore, or as a result.

100
00:04:18,423 --> 00:04:19,362
That's D.

101
00:04:19,382 --> 00:04:21,005
Nevertheless is the trap.

102
00:04:21,025 --> 00:04:24,291
The phrase unlike most substances
sounds like a contrast.

103
00:04:24,311 --> 00:04:27,469
But that contrast is
inside the first sentence.

104
00:04:27,489 --> 00:04:30,005
Between the two sentences,
it's cause and effect.

105
00:04:30,025 --> 00:04:33,755
Nevertheless would mean ice
floats despite being less dense,

106
00:04:33,775 --> 00:04:35,240
which is backwards.

107
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:36,453
Question three.

108
00:04:36,473 --> 00:04:40,294
Some animals turn objects from
their surroundings into tools.

109
00:04:40,455 --> 00:04:44,149
blank New Caledonian crows
break twigs off bushes,

110
00:04:44,169 --> 00:04:49,348
trim them into sticks, and use the sticks
to pull insects out of holes in logs.

111
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,737
Pause and try it.

112
00:04:53,981 --> 00:04:56,140
The first sentence is a general claim:

113
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:58,267
some animals make tools.

114
00:04:58,374 --> 00:05:01,730
The second is one specific case: crows.

115
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:04,925
General, then specific, means example.

116
00:05:04,945 --> 00:05:07,052
The answer is B, for instance.

117
00:05:07,148 --> 00:05:08,863
In other words is the tempting one.

118
00:05:09,148 --> 00:05:12,057
But in other words means the next
sentence says the same thing again.

119
00:05:12,077 --> 00:05:13,521
This one doesn't restate the claim.

120
00:05:13,541 --> 00:05:16,291
It adds a new, narrower case.

121
00:05:16,325 --> 00:05:17,539
Question four.

122
00:05:17,717 --> 00:05:22,090
The Svalbard Global Seed Vault, built
inside a mountain on a remote Arctic

123
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:26,805
island, stores backup copies of seeds
from gene banks around the world.

124
00:05:26,825 --> 00:05:31,412
The vault sits well above sea level, so
it should stay dry even if sea levels

125
00:05:31,432 --> 00:05:32,412
rise.

126
00:05:32,432 --> 00:05:36,912
blank the permafrost and thick rock
surrounding the vault would keep the seeds

127
00:05:36,932 --> 00:05:39,182
frozen even if the power failed.

128
00:05:39,228 --> 00:05:40,585
Pause and try it.

129
00:05:43,829 --> 00:05:47,416
Before the blank: one way
the vault protects the seeds.

130
00:05:47,436 --> 00:05:49,400
After it: a second way.

131
00:05:49,472 --> 00:05:52,023
Two separate points,
pointing the same direction.

132
00:05:52,043 --> 00:05:53,059
That's addition.

133
00:05:53,079 --> 00:05:55,614
The answer is B, additionally.

134
00:05:55,649 --> 00:05:57,414
For this reason is the trap.

135
00:05:57,434 --> 00:05:59,879
Being above sea level
doesn't cause the permafrost.

136
00:05:59,899 --> 00:06:02,985
Two facts side by side
aren't cause and effect.

137
00:06:03,005 --> 00:06:04,950
And nonetheless would need a contrast,

138
00:06:04,970 --> 00:06:06,021
which isn't there.

139
00:06:06,041 --> 00:06:09,449
Instead would mean one
protection replaces the other,

140
00:06:09,469 --> 00:06:11,220
but the vault has both.

141
00:06:11,306 --> 00:06:12,715
Question five.

142
00:06:12,735 --> 00:06:17,608
In nineteen twenty-eight, Alexander
Fleming noticed that a mold growing in one

143
00:06:17,628 --> 00:06:21,306
of his laboratory dishes had
killed the bacteria around it.

144
00:06:21,395 --> 00:06:26,340
blank in nineteen forty, a team at
the University of Oxford showed that a

145
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:29,410
purified form of the
substance the mold produced,

146
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:33,860
penicillin, could protect mice
from a deadly bacterial infection.

147
00:06:33,908 --> 00:06:35,265
Pause and try it.

148
00:06:38,509 --> 00:06:40,009
The dates are your clue.

149
00:06:40,045 --> 00:06:42,759
Nineteen twenty-eight,
then nineteen forty.

150
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:46,131
One event happened, and
then, twelve years on,

151
00:06:46,151 --> 00:06:47,239
another one did.

152
00:06:47,259 --> 00:06:48,402
That's sequence.

153
00:06:48,509 --> 00:06:51,009
The answer is A, later.

154
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:54,867
Instead would mean the Oxford
work replaced Fleming's discovery.

155
00:06:54,887 --> 00:06:55,724
It built on it.

156
00:06:55,744 --> 00:06:58,545
The experiment isn't an
example of his observation,

157
00:06:58,565 --> 00:07:00,260
and it isn't a restatement either.

158
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,529
It's a new event.

159
00:07:01,586 --> 00:07:02,836
Now the traps.

160
00:07:02,907 --> 00:07:06,173
Trap one: two choices
that do the same job.

161
00:07:06,193 --> 00:07:09,316
If therefore and as a
result are both choices,

162
00:07:09,336 --> 00:07:10,565
they mean the same thing.

163
00:07:10,585 --> 00:07:12,744
They can't both be the one right answer,

164
00:07:12,764 --> 00:07:14,898
so usually neither is.

165
00:07:14,918 --> 00:07:18,470
Trap two: the however
versus therefore flip.

166
00:07:18,490 --> 00:07:19,541
They're opposites.

167
00:07:19,561 --> 00:07:22,183
Therefore says the next
idea is what you'd expect.

168
00:07:22,203 --> 00:07:24,684
However says it goes
against what you'd expect.

169
00:07:24,704 --> 00:07:28,632
If you're stuck between them, ask:
is the second sentence a surprise?

170
00:07:28,703 --> 00:07:32,683
Trap three: grabbing a contrast word
because you noticed a contrast somewhere in

171
00:07:32,703 --> 00:07:33,504
the passage.

172
00:07:33,524 --> 00:07:36,560
Only the relationship
across the blank counts.

173
00:07:36,636 --> 00:07:37,866
Question six.

174
00:07:37,886 --> 00:07:42,437
In nineteen thirty-five, cane toads were
brought to Australia to control beetles

175
00:07:42,457 --> 00:07:44,671
that were damaging sugarcane crops.

176
00:07:44,796 --> 00:07:48,671
blank the toads had no
noticeable effect on the beetles.

177
00:07:48,723 --> 00:07:50,080
Pause and try it.

178
00:07:54,324 --> 00:07:56,768
The toads were brought in
to control the beetles.

179
00:07:56,788 --> 00:07:59,019
Then they had no noticeable effect.

180
00:07:59,039 --> 00:08:00,360
Is that what you'd expect?

181
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:00,947
No.

182
00:08:00,967 --> 00:08:02,269
The plan failed.

183
00:08:02,289 --> 00:08:04,376
That's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

184
00:08:04,396 --> 00:08:05,161
however.

185
00:08:05,181 --> 00:08:06,860
The answer is C.

186
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:08,438
Now look at A and B.

187
00:08:08,652 --> 00:08:11,026
Therefore and as a result do the same job,

188
00:08:11,046 --> 00:08:13,097
so they can't both be right.

189
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:15,668
And they'd both say the
plan caused the failure,

190
00:08:15,688 --> 00:08:16,954
which makes no sense.

191
00:08:16,974 --> 00:08:18,913
For example doesn't fit either.

192
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:19,933
Here's the flip.

193
00:08:20,183 --> 00:08:24,540
If the first sentence had said the
toads couldn't reach the beetles,

194
00:08:24,612 --> 00:08:26,341
then therefore would work.

195
00:08:26,361 --> 00:08:29,485
The words around the blank
decide the transition,

196
00:08:29,505 --> 00:08:30,719
not the topic.

197
00:08:30,771 --> 00:08:32,287
Last one, and it's harder.

198
00:08:32,307 --> 00:08:35,037
The first telegraph cable laid
across the Atlantic Ocean,

199
00:08:35,057 --> 00:08:39,842
completed in eighteen fifty-eight, stopped
working after only about three weeks.

200
00:08:39,994 --> 00:08:44,697
blank the short-lived cable proved that
an undersea cable could carry messages

201
00:08:44,717 --> 00:08:46,967
between Europe and North America.

202
00:08:46,989 --> 00:08:47,647
Pause and try it.

203
00:08:47,667 --> 00:08:49,167
Take a little longer on this one.

204
00:08:53,363 --> 00:08:55,221
The cable failed fast.

205
00:08:55,649 --> 00:08:57,451
But it still proved the idea worked.

206
00:08:57,471 --> 00:09:01,184
The relationship is: despite that.

207
00:09:01,292 --> 00:09:04,078
So the answer is B, nevertheless.

208
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:08,768
Here's why in contrast is wrong, even
though it's also a contrast word.

209
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,390
In contrast compares two different things,

210
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:13,820
like two planets or two telescopes.

211
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,320
This passage has only
one thing, the cable.

212
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:18,041
There's nothing to compare it to.

213
00:09:18,061 --> 00:09:21,113
Consequently would mean the
failure caused the proof.

214
00:09:21,133 --> 00:09:23,434
And nothing here is an example.

215
00:09:23,454 --> 00:09:27,847
So the rule from earlier
needs one adjustment.

216
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:29,684
True synonyms are both out.

217
00:09:29,704 --> 00:09:33,704
But two words from the same family
can still do different jobs.

218
00:09:33,724 --> 00:09:35,490
Here's the method on one card.

219
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:36,811
Cover the choices.

220
00:09:36,831 --> 00:09:39,633
Read the sentence before
and after the blank.

221
00:09:39,653 --> 00:09:40,810
Name the relationship.

222
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:43,224
Then match the group, and read it back in.

223
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:47,009
If you're stuck between two
choices, ask the sharper question.

224
00:09:47,029 --> 00:09:50,330
Is the second idea
expected, or a surprise?

225
00:09:50,350 --> 00:09:54,437
Are two things being compared, or
is one idea true despite another?

226
00:09:54,457 --> 00:09:56,279
That usually breaks the tie.

227
00:09:56,377 --> 00:09:57,179
Recap.

228
00:09:57,199 --> 00:10:00,699
Transitions test
relationships, not vocabulary.

229
00:10:00,806 --> 00:10:03,499
Predict the relationship
first, then find it.

230
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:07,428
Watch for same-job pairs, the
however versus therefore flip,

231
00:10:07,448 --> 00:10:09,734
and contrast versus concession.

232
00:10:09,757 --> 00:10:13,416
For more practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter for

233
00:10:13,436 --> 00:10:16,222
transitions under Expression of Ideas.

234
00:10:16,262 --> 00:10:19,849
All the questions in this video
were written for this video,

235
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:22,135
in the style of the real test.

236
00:10:22,155 --> 00:10:24,027
If this helped, subscribe.

237
00:10:24,047 --> 00:10:27,725
Next up: command of evidence
questions with tables and graphs.
